get.description:
super_admin may list all users; admin may list member users only;
member is always forbidden. A role filter cannot expand the caller's
scope; an out-of-scope filter is rejected (FR-001, FR-002).

post.description:
super_admin may create admin or member; admin may create member only;
member is forbidden. The password is accepted for credential setup but
never returned or persisted in plaintext (FR-002, FR-003).

admin may change status for member only; super_admin may change status
for admin or member. The final active super_admin cannot be disabled,
and a disabled user cannot authenticate afterwards (FR-002, FR-003).
